1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,524
Paw Twin gives family members a shared pet record, helping them coordinate everyday care.

2
00:00:05,724 --> 00:00:11,547
This local review follows Mochi through two independent accounts, using fictional demonstration data.

3
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:21,583
The owner records sample weights of one point two and one point three five kilograms, seven days apart.

4
00:00:21,783 --> 00:00:27,277
The weekly report calculates a hundred fifty gram increase, or twelve point five percent.

5
00:00:31,217 --> 00:00:37,795
The report exposes its time window, record identifiers, and version, so people can inspect the calculation.

6
00:00:37,995 --> 00:00:45,038
Missing intake remains unrecorded, coverage is incomplete, and these sample measurements provide no medical diagnosis.

7
00:00:49,017 --> 00:00:54,300
The owner saves a preference candidate: Mochi likes a feather toy and rests after meals.

8
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,513
Only explicit confirmation shares this database memory, while stored text never becomes an instruction.

9
00:01:04,483 --> 00:01:09,867
After a separate login, the carer asks what Mochi likes through the labelled Alexa web simulator.

10
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:15,840
The response uses confirmed context and local rules; no live Alexa or model call occurs.

11
00:01:19,817 --> 00:01:24,320
The owner writes a proposal to rest after meals, then play with the feather toy.

12
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:30,104
Explicit owner confirmation creates a shared manual care task, with no feeder execution.

13
00:01:34,083 --> 00:01:38,042
The carer claims the task and records completion through the second account.

14
00:01:38,242 --> 00:01:44,495
This manual record proves an account action, without establishing physical device activity or real world care.

15
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:52,892
Household activity visibly attributes the claim and completion events to the carer.

16
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:59,455
The captured evidence verifies the actual completing account identifier, keeping labels separate from permissions.

17
00:02:03,417 --> 00:02:08,785
The daily report now counts one completed manual care task, with none pending or overdue.

18
00:02:08,985 --> 00:02:14,524
Intake remains unrecorded and daily weight change remains unknown, preserving missing outcomes.

19
00:02:18,483 --> 00:02:22,612
After the owner deletes the preference, the carer asks again in the App.

20
00:02:22,812 --> 00:02:28,460
The next answer has no confirmed preference and an empty source list, showing deletion took effect.

21
00:02:32,417 --> 00:02:38,465
This is a local rules review, with database memory, manual care, and simulated Alexa and hardware.

22
00:02:38,665 --> 00:02:46,388
AWS validation remains pending account verification, so this demo establishes neither live model behavior nor cloud readiness.
